    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/clinical-trials-contracts-administrator-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia-unisc-southbank-health-hub-morayfield-e336005e-65bb-4837-a5bf-3f4d5a823939": {
      "title": "Clinical Trials Contracts Administrator",
      "description": "Clinical Trials Contracts Administrator - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC SouthBank, QLD, Australia - Health Hub Morayfield, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Clinical Trials Contracts Administrator 19-31 Dickson Road, Health Hub Morayfield, QLD, Australia, 4506 32 Cordelia Street, UniSC SouthBank, QLD, Australia, 4101 90 Sippy Downs Drive, UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Administration / Admin Support Casual Professional Clinical Trials Individual contributor L5 $54.75 per hour (casual) Show More Show Less Casual Add to favourites View favourites UniSC Clinical Trials Centre | UniSC Sippy Downs, Sunshine Coast, Health Hub Morayfield or UniSC Southbank, Brisbane Level 5, $54.75 per hour plus 12% superannuation Casual opportunity The Opportunity UniSC Clinical Trials builds the region’s collective clinical research capacity and delivers innovative and regionally relevant research in collaboration with healthcare professionals, industry partners and research stakeholders. The Clinical Trials Contracts Administrator contributes to this mission by providing administrative and governance support for the review, negotiation and finalisation of contracts and agreements that underpin high-quality clinical research across UniSC’s clinical trials network. Join UniSC and contribute to a university committed to transforming lives through learning, knowledge and meaningful community impact. In this role, you will assist with the review, negotiation and finalisation of clinical trial agreements, working closely with internal teams and external partners to support efficient, compliant and well-governed clinical trial activities. For more information, please visit us online: UniSC Clinical Trials You will assist in the triage of clinical trial contracts and agreements to assess due diligence requirements and support administrative contract management; support the governance and administration of clinical trial contracts and agreements from initial negotiation with external partners through to execution; provide comprehensive administrative support to finalise contracts and agreements, facilitate internal approvals and circulate documentation for execution using the Adobe Sign electronic signature platform; perform due diligence reviews of contracts and agreements and, where appropriate, coordinate requests for review by UniSC Legal; support researchers and internal stakeholders to understand contractual milestones, key obligations and internal requirements; work collaboratively with teams across Business Development, Finance and Project Management, as well as sponsors, contract research organisations and third-party vendors, to support contractual processes and timely clinical trial establishment; and support the maintenance of the UniSC Clinical Trials contract template library, including liaising with UniSC Legal regarding updates to templates as required. About you You are a highly organised and detail-oriented administrator with strong written communication skills and an interest in supporting clinical research. You are comfortable managing complex documentation, coordinating approval workflows and working with a diverse range of internal and external stakeholders. You bring sound judgement, strong digital literacy and the ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail. You enjoy working both independently and collaboratively and can contribute to efficient, compliant and well-managed contractual processes within a busy clinical trials environment. You will possess: Completion of a degree, or an associate diploma with at least two years of subsequent relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant knowledge, training and experience; Sound knowledge of ICH Good Clinical Practice and applicable regulations; Excellent written and verbal communication skills, combined with strong attention to detail; A sound understanding of privacy principles governing health information; The ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a multidisciplinary team; High-level digital literacy, including experience using databases and Microsoft Word and Excel; and Strong organisational and administrative skills, with the ability to manage documentation, workflows and competing priorities accurately and efficiently. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au All applications must be lodged through the UniSC Careers website. UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 13 September 2026. Your completed application must include: a resume , noting your application will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the job advertisement. There will be opportunity within the application form to also include supporting documentation should you wish. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Alishia Ballintine Senior Manager, Legal and Compliance, UniSC Clinical Trials Email: aballintine@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Clinical Practice Educator, Nutrition and Dietetics UniSC Sunshine Coast. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic, LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super, School of Health Shape the future of nutrition and dietetics through high-quality clinical education, student supervision and meaningful industry partnerships. Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Caboolture. UniSC Fraser Coast. UniSC Gympie. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Join a growing UniSC team, with multiple newly created opportunities supporting the expansion of our Nursing and Midwifery programs. Bring your clinical or technical expertise and make a difference to the next generation of health professionals. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help students turn learning into real-world impact through meaningful industry experiences that shape future careers. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help shape meaningful industry experiences that transform student futures. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
