    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/casual-chef-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-australia": {
      "title": "Casual Chef",
      "description": "Casual Chef - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Casual Chef 1 Moreton Parade, UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Campus Development and Services Casual Professional Food and Beverage L3 $43.98 per hour (casual) Show More Show Less Casual Add to favourites View favourites Venues and Catering | UniSC Moreton Bay, Petrie Level 3 - $43.98 per hour plus 12% employer superannuation Casual appointment The Opportunity The Venues & Catering team within Campus Development and Services deliver high-quality food services across UniSC campuses, including cafés, functions, conferences and major university events. The team works collaboratively to ensure consistency in food quality, service delivery, and customer experience across all locations. This role is a casual opportunity supporting kitchen operations at our Moreton Bay campus. As a Casual Chef, you will contribute to the preparation and delivery of high-quality food services, ensuring efficient operations and exceptional customer satisfaction. This opportunity offers flexible hours in line with business requirements, including weekdays, weekends and peak event periods. You will: prepare and present food to a high professional standard in line with menu specifications and brand expectations; support catering delivery for conferences, corporate events, graduations and internal functions; maintain strict food safety and hygiene standards in accordance with HACCP and relevant legislation; ensure efficient kitchen operations, including stock rotation, portion control and waste minimisation; collaborate with chefs, front-of-house staff and events teams to deliver seamless service; assist with menu preparation, including accommodating dietary and cultural requirements; operate kitchen equipment safely and effectively; maintain cleanliness and organisation of kitchen and storage areas; and prepare and place daily menu orders in line with customer demand. About you: You are a motivated and reliable chef with a strong commitment to quality, safety and customer service. You thrive in a fast-paced kitchen environment and bring a collaborative approach to team-based service delivery. You will possess: a relevant trade qualification (Certificate III in Commercial Cookery or equivalent); demonstrated experience in a commercial kitchen environment; strong knowledge of food safety standards and best practices; ability to work efficiently in a high-volume, fast-paced environment; flexibility to work varied hours, including early mornings, evenings and weekends; strong teamwork and communication skills; ability to travel between UniSC campuses as required; and relevant food safety certifications. Experience in event or large-scale catering, along with knowledge of diverse cuisines and dietary requirements, will be highly regarded. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. All applications must be lodged through the Careers at UniSC website. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 13 September 2026. Your completed application must include: a resume, noting your application will be reviewed in alignment to the specified Selection Criteria as outlined within the advertisement. We will be reviewing applications and contacting suitable candidates throughout the duration of this advertisement. We strongly encourage you to submit your interest as soon as possible. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at : Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Ursula Dodds Venues and Catering Manager Email: udodds@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We’re all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. While we’re not the largest university, we are one of the fastest growing in Australia, now with over 2,000 staff across five campuses in South East Queensland and an expanding presence in major capital cities, and we’re making a big impact every day through ground-breaking research, a strong commitment to sustainability, high-performance sport, and award-winning alumni. We are committed to delivering high-quality research and teaching that address major global and regional challenges, with established and emerging strengths in sustainability, environmental systems, biodiversity, aquaculture, preventative health and regional resilience. Our research excellence is internationally recognised through strong performance in global benchmarking, including leading rankings in the 2025 Times Higher Education (THE) Impact Rankings for “Zero Hunger,” “Climate Action” and “Life on Land.” UniSC is also recognised for its teaching excellence, with a strong emphasis on student success, innovative and engaging learning experiences, and strong graduate outcomes that equip learners to make meaningful contributions in their chosen fields. As the only university operating within three UNESCO Biosphere Reserves and a UNESCO World Heritage Site, UniSC is uniquely positioned to leverage its natural environment to advance impactful research, teaching and partnerships that support sustainable futures, with sustainability embedded across all aspects of our teaching, research and operations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment that encourages continuous professional development and provides the tools and resources to grow your career. We value the contributions of every team member and the role they play in our culture and success. We’re not afraid to do things differently, and we’re looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team working together to make a meaningful difference to local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Clinical Practice Educator, Nutrition and Dietetics UniSC Sunshine Coast. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic, LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super, School of Health Shape the future of nutrition and dietetics through high-quality clinical education, student supervision and meaningful industry partnerships. Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Caboolture. UniSC Fraser Coast. UniSC Gympie. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Join a growing UniSC team, with multiple newly created opportunities supporting the expansion of our Nursing and Midwifery programs. Bring your clinical or technical expertise and make a difference to the next generation of health professionals. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help students turn learning into real-world impact through meaningful industry experiences that shape future careers. Work Integrated Learning (WIL) Placement Officer UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, Administration / Admin Support, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help shape meaningful industry experiences that transform student futures. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
